## 5. Redis Key Naming Scheme

| Pattern | TTL | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `dashboard:kpi:payload` | 60s | n8n KPI object for Dashboard Data Endpoint |
| `dash:<role>:<qs\|default>` | 30s | Vercel `/api/dashboard-data` response cache |
| `authfail:dashboard:<clinicId>:<ip>` | 900s | n8n PIN / agency-key brute-force counter |
| `ratelimit:dashboard:<ip>` | 300s | n8n dashboard request window (max 30) |
| `ratelimit:login:<ip>` | 900s | Vercel `/api/auth` login window (max 5) |
| `errmon:dedup:<dedupKey>` | 300s | Error-monitor Slack dedup (`SET NX`) |

Slot mutex (Concierge / waitlist): `SET <lockKey> 1 NX EX <ttl>` via Upstash REST. Missing Redis on a **lock** path is a hard error. Missing Redis on a **cache** path is a miss.

**Env names — do not unify**

| Runtime | URL | Token |
|---|---|---|
| Vercel | `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL` | `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN` |
| n8n (`$vars` / `$env`) | `REDIS_CONNECTION_URL` | `REDIS_REST_TOKEN` |

