## 10. Error Handling Conventions

**Vercel proxies**

```json
{ "ok": false, "error": "Webhook not configured" }
```

| HTTP | When |
|---|---|
| 401 | Missing/invalid JWT |
| 405 | Wrong method |
| 429 | Login rate limit |
| 500 | Missing server auth config (agency key) |
| 502 | Upstream timeout / fetch failure |
| 503 | Webhook env missing |

Do not put n8n HTML error pages in `error` as if they were KPI payloads.

**n8n (Dashboard Data Endpoint and shared `error_handler.js`)**

Internal throw prefixes: `AUTH_FAIL:…`, `RATE_LIMIT:…`. Client body:

```json
{
  "ok": false,
  "error": "Unauthorized | Too Many Requests | Service temporarily unavailable",
  "message": "human-readable French or English staff message",
  "timestamp": "fr-MA Africa/Casablanca",
  "trace_id": "err-…"
}
```

HTTP: 401 / 429 / 503. Never return stack traces.

KPI success shape (plus `last_updated`, `schema_warnings`, cache flags):

`patients_today`, `no_shows`, `revenue_today`, `new_patients`, `accepted_plans`, `pending_plans`, `hour_08` … `hour_18`.

